  "subtitle": "The self-service ticket vending machine whose output is a physical notched card that IS the data",
  "why_scout_cares": "A public self-service terminal where the interface contracts down to a physical ritual: press destination and ticket-type buttons, feed coins, watch a continuous-roll cardstock ticket get cut to length and drop out — with the fare data literally punched into the notches of the card itself. No magnetic stripe, no software lookup at the outlet: the ticket is the data, printed and cut on the spot. Distinct from every terminal in the collection and a fresh member of the physical-token-as-data family.",
